#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah anggaran fasa {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section of the lesson explains the *phase estimation problem*.\n"
"We'll begin with a short discussion of the *spectral theorem* from linear algebra, and then move on to a statement of the phase estimation problem itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian pelajaran ini menerangkan *masalah anggaran fasa*.\n"
"Kita akan mulakan dengan perbincangan ringkas tentang *teorem spektral* daripada aljabar linear, kemudian beralih kepada pernyataan masalah anggaran fasa itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "Teorem spektral {#spectral-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *spectral theorem* is an important fact from linear algebra that states that matrices of a certain type, called *normal matrices,* can be expressed in a simple and useful way.\n"
"We'll only need this theorem for unitary matrices in this lesson, but down the road in this series we'll apply it to Hermitian matrices as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Teorem spektral* adalah fakta penting daripada aljabar linear yang menyatakan bahawa matriks jenis tertentu, yang dipanggil *matriks normal,* boleh dinyatakan dengan cara yang mudah dan berguna.\n"
"Kita hanya memerlukan teorem ini untuk matriks unitari dalam pelajaran ini, tetapi kemudian dalam siri ini kita akan menggunakannya untuk matriks Hermitian juga.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Normal matrices {#normal-matrices}"
msgstr "Matriks normal {#normal-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $M$ with complex number entries is said to be a *normal* matrix if it commutes with its conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks persegi $M$ dengan entri nombor kompleks dikatakan sebagai matriks *normal* jika ia bertukar ganti dengan transpos konjugatnya:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Every unitary matrix $U$ is normal because\n"
msgstr "Setiap matriks unitari $U$ adalah normal kerana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hermitian matrices, which are matrices that equal their own conjugate transpose, are another important class of normal matrices.\n"
"If $H$ is a Hermitian matrix, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks Hermitian, iaitu matriks yang sama dengan transpos konjugatnya sendiri, adalah kelas lain matriks normal yang penting.\n"
"Jika $H$ adalah matriks Hermitian, maka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so $H$ is normal.\n"
msgstr "jadi $H$ adalah normal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every square matrix is normal.\n"
"For instance, this matrix isn't normal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak setiap matriks persegi adalah normal.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, matriks ini bukan normal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(This is a simple but great example of a matrix that's often very helpful to consider.)\n"
"It isn't normal because\n"
msgstr ""
"(Ini adalah contoh mudah tetapi hebat tentang matriks yang sering sangat berguna untuk dipertimbangkan.)\n"
"Ia bukan normal kerana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while\n"
msgstr "manakala\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement {#theorem-statement}"
msgstr "Pernyataan teorem {#theorem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now here's a statement of the spectral theorem.\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah pernyataan teorem spektral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a normal $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $N$-dimensional complex vectors $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorem\">\n"
"Teorem spektral: Biarkan $M$ adalah matriks kompleks normal $N\\times N$.\n"
"Terdapat asas ortonormal bagi vektor kompleks $N$-dimensi $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ bersama-sama dengan nombor kompleks $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ sedemikian rupa sehingga\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The expression of a matrix in the form\n"
msgstr "Ungkapan sebuah matriks dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is commonly called a *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Notice that if $M$ is a normal matrix expressed in the form $(1),$ then the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"biasanya dipanggil *penguraian spektral*.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa jika $M$ adalah matriks normal yang dinyatakan dalam bentuk $(1),$ maka persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"must be true for every $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"This is a consequence of the fact that $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ is orthonormal:\n"
msgstr ""
"mestilah benar untuk setiap $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"Ini adalah akibat daripada fakta bahawa $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ adalah ortonormal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, each number $\\lambda_j$ is an *eigenvalue* of $M$ and "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* corresponding to that "
"eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, setiap nombor $\\lambda_j$ adalah *nilai eigen* bagi $M$ dan "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ adalah *vektor eigen* yang berkaitan dengan nilai "
"eigen tersebut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.\n"
"Let\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh 1**.\n"
"Biarkan\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  which is normal.\n"
"  The theorem implies that $\\mathbb{I}$ can be written in the form $(1)$ for some choice of $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ and $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  There are multiple choices that work, including\n"
msgstr ""
"  yang merupakan normal.\n"
"  Teorem ini menyiratkan bahawa $\\mathbb{I}$ boleh ditulis dalam bentuk $(1)$ untuk sesetengah pilihan $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ dan $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  Terdapat pelbagai pilihan yang berfungsi, termasuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Notice that the theorem does not say that the complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ are\n"
"  distinct — we can have the same complex number repeated, which is necessary for this example.\n"
"  These choices work because\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Perhatikan bahawa teorem ini tidak mengatakan bahawa nombor kompleks $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ adalah\n"
"  berbeza — kita boleh mempunyai nombor kompleks yang sama berulang, yang diperlukan untuk contoh ini.\n"
"  Pilihan-pilihan ini berfungsi kerana\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Indeed, we could choose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ to be *any* orthonormal basis and the\n"
"  equation will be true. For instance,\n"
msgstr ""
"  Malah, kita boleh memilih $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ sebagai *mana-mana* asas ortonormal dan\n"
"  persamaan akan benar. Sebagai contoh,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 2**.\n"
"Consider a Hadamard operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh 2**.\n"
"Pertimbangkan operasi Hadamard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is a unitary matrix, so it is normal. The spectral theorem implies that $H$ can be written in the\n"
"  form $(1),$ and in particular we have\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ini adalah matriks unitari, jadi ia adalah normal. Teorem spektral menyiratkan bahawa $H$ boleh ditulis dalam\n"
"  bentuk $(1),$ dan khususnya kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  where\n"
msgstr "  di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  More explicitly,\n"
msgstr "  Dengan lebih eksplisit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  We can check that this decomposition is correct by performing the required"
" calculations:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kita boleh menyemak bahawa penguraian ini betul dengan melakukan pengiraan"
" yang diperlukan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the first example above reveals, there can be some freedom in how eigenvectors are selected.\n"
"There is, however, no freedom at all in how the eigenvalues are chosen, except for their ordering:\n"
"the same $N$ complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N,$ which can include repetitions of the same complex number, will always occur in the equation $(1)$ for a given choice of a matrix $M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang didedahkan oleh contoh pertama di atas, terdapat sedikit kebebasan dalam bagaimana vektor eigen dipilih.\n"
"Namun, tiada kebebasan sama sekali dalam bagaimana nilai eigen dipilih, kecuali untuk pengurutannya:\n"
"nombor kompleks yang sama $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N,$ yang boleh merangkumi pengulangan nombor kompleks yang sama, akan sentiasa muncul dalam persamaan $(1)$ untuk pilihan matriks $M$ yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's focus in on unitary matrices.\n"
"Suppose we have a complex number $\\lambda$ and a non-zero vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita fokus kepada matriks unitari.\n"
"Andaikan kita mempunyai nombor kompleks $\\lambda$ dan vektor bukan sifar $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang memenuhi persamaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $U$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an "
"eigenvector corresponding to this eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, $\\lambda$ adalah nilai eigen bagi $U$ dan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ "
"adalah vektor eigen yang berkaitan dengan nilai eigen ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary matrices preserve Euclidean norm, and so we conclude the following "
"from $(2).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks unitari memelihara norma Euclidean, dan oleh itu kita menyimpulkan "
"perkara berikut daripada $(2).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The condition that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is non-zero implies that $\\bigl\\|"
" \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ so we can cancel it from both sides "
"to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat bahawa $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ adalah bukan sifar menyiratkan bahawa "
"$\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ jadi kita boleh "
"membatalkannya dari kedua-dua belah untuk memperoleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This reveals that eigenvalues of unitary matrices must always have absolute "
"value equal to one, so they lie on the *unit circle.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini mendedahkan bahawa nilai eigen bagi matriks unitari mestilah sentiasa "
"mempunyai nilai mutlak yang sama dengan satu, jadi ia terletak pada *bulatan"
" unit.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(The symbol $\\mathbb{T}$ is a common name for the complex unit circle. The "
"name $S^1$ is also common.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Simbol $\\mathbb{T}$ adalah nama lazim untuk bulatan unit kompleks. Nama "
"$S^1$ juga lazim.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Phase estimation problem statement {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"
msgstr ""
"Pernyataan masalah anggaran fasa {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the *phase estimation problem*, we're given a quantum state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of $n$ qubits, along with a unitary quantum circuit that acts on $n$ qubits.\n"
"We're *promised* that $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of the unitary matrix $U$ that describes the action of the circuit, and our goal is to compute or approximate the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ to which $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ corresponds.\n"
"More precisely, because $\\lambda$ lies on the complex unit circle, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam *masalah anggaran fasa*, kita diberi keadaan kuantum $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ bagi $n$ Qubit, bersama-sama dengan litar kuantum unitari yang bertindak ke atas $n$ Qubit.\n"
"Kita *dijanjikan* bahawa $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ adalah vektor eigen bagi matriks unitari $U$ yang menggambarkan tindakan litar, dan matlamat kita adalah untuk mengira atau menganggarkan nilai eigen $\\lambda$ yang berkaitan dengan $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Lebih tepat lagi, kerana $\\lambda$ terletak pada bulatan unit kompleks, kita boleh menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a unique real number $\\theta$ satisfying $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"The goal of the problem is to compute or approximate this real number $\\theta.$\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk nombor nyata unik $\\theta$ yang memenuhi $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"Matlamat masalah ini adalah untuk mengira atau menganggarkan nombor nyata $\\theta$ ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Phase estimation problem\">\n"
"Input: A unitary quantum circuit for an $n$-qubit operation $U$ along with an $n$-qubit quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promise: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U$ \\\n"
"Output: an approximation to the number $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfying $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah anggaran fasa\">\n"
"Input: Litar kuantum unitari untuk operasi $U$ bagi $n$-Qubit bersama-sama dengan keadaan kuantum $n$-Qubit $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Janji: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ adalah vektor eigen bagi $U$ \\\n"
"Output: penghampiran kepada nombor $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ yang memenuhi $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few remarks about this problem statement:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah beberapa catatan mengenai pernyataan masalah ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The phase estimation problem is different from other problems we've seen so "
"far in the course in that the input includes a quantum state. Typically we "
"focus on problems having classical inputs and outputs, but nothing prevents "
"us from considering quantum state inputs like this. In terms of its "
"practical relevance, the phase estimation problem is typically encountered "
"as a *subproblem* inside of a larger computation, like we'll see in the "
"context of integer factorization later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah anggaran fasa berbeza daripada masalah lain yang telah kita lihat "
"setakat ini dalam kursus kerana input merangkumi keadaan kuantum. Biasanya "
"kita fokus kepada masalah yang mempunyai input dan output klasik, tetapi "
"tiada yang menghalang kita daripada mempertimbangkan input keadaan kuantum "
"seperti ini. Dari segi relevansi praktikalnya, masalah anggaran fasa "
"biasanya ditemui sebagai *submasalah* dalam pengiraan yang lebih besar, "
"seperti yang akan kita lihat dalam konteks pemfaktoran integer kemudian "
"dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The statement of the phase estimation problem above isn't specific about "
"what constitutes an approximation of $\\theta,$ but we can formulate more "
"precise problem statements depending on our needs and interests. In the "
"context of integer factorization, we'll demand a very precise approximation "
"to $\\theta,$ but in other cases we might be satisfied with a very rough "
"approximation. We'll discuss shortly how the precision we require affects "
"the computational cost of a solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pernyataan masalah anggaran fasa di atas tidak khusus tentang apa yang "
"merupakan penghampiran kepada $\\theta,$ tetapi kita boleh merumuskan "
"pernyataan masalah yang lebih tepat bergantung kepada keperluan dan minat "
"kita. Dalam konteks pemfaktoran integer, kita akan memerlukan penghampiran "
"yang sangat tepat kepada $\\theta,$ tetapi dalam kes lain kita mungkin "
"berpuas hati dengan penghampiran yang sangat kasar. Kita akan bincangkan "
"tidak lama lagi bagaimana ketepatan yang kita perlukan mempengaruhi kos "
"pengiraan sesuatu penyelesaian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that as we go from $\\theta = 0$ toward $\\theta = 1$ in the phase "
"estimation problem, we're going all the way around the unit circle, starting"
" from $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ and moving counter-clockwise toward "
"$e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$ That is, when we reach $\\theta = 1$ we're back "
"where we started at $\\theta = 0.$ So, as we consider the accuracy of "
"approximations, choices of $\\theta$ near $1$ should be considered as being "
"near $0.$ For example, an approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ should be "
"considered as being within $1/1000$ of $\\theta = 0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa apabila kita bergerak dari $\\theta = 0$ ke arah $\\theta "
"= 1$ dalam masalah anggaran fasa, kita mengelilingi seluruh bulatan unit, "
"bermula dari $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ dan bergerak lawan jam ke arah "
"$e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$ Iaitu, apabila kita mencapai $\\theta = 1$ kita "
"kembali ke tempat asal pada $\\theta = 0.$ Jadi, apabila kita "
"mempertimbangkan ketepatan penghampiran, pilihan $\\theta$ yang hampir "
"kepada $1$ harus dianggap sebagai hampir kepada $0.$ Sebagai contoh, "
"penghampiran $\\theta = 0.999$ harus dianggap sebagai berada dalam jarak "
"$1/1000$ daripada $\\theta = 0.$\n"
